  "acceptance_disposition": {
    "A123": "Both ordinary peers are concretely owned immediately at spawn. Transferred raw handles in controls become owners before the completion future is polled. Its cancellation drops both owners and requests abort.",
    "A125": "Operation Err reaches the existing pair finisher. Both stop results are observed concurrently and nested FixtureFailures preserve original primary and both actual completed cleanup errors; ordinary success also observes both typed outputs.",
    "A129": "LocalSocksDeadline retains the original operation prefix and actual Elapsed as Error::source. Inner operation errors and successful results still pass through."
  },
  "findings": [],
  "limitations": [
    "Source approval is not compilation or runtime proof; parent must execute the 19 methods and ordinary consumer/lint/MSRV checks.",
    "ConnectionPeer Drop requests abort but does not synchronously join. Explicit stop waits at most five seconds and retains actual timeout/error; the outer five-second bound can interrupt cleanup. No unconditional drain or permanent OS resource-release guarantee is claimed.",
    "The peer child intentionally retains raw launchers inside driven_route to exercise transfer into the actual completion helper. Its ordinary setup-error branch aborts/joins both, but outer cancellation or assertion panic during this baseline setup is not newly made unconditionally owned by this remedy.",
    "Completed-object controls wait for actual task destruction before helper entry; this validates ready/completed error retention, not retention of errors that have not happened when cancellation is requested.",
    "FixtureFailures Error::source exposes its primary. The cleanup object remains separately inspectable; the control recursively checks both concrete fields. No claim that a linear source traversal exposes every secondary error.",
    "Target controls observe literal wire ATYP and forwarding to a held IPv4 loopback origin; they do not prove live DNS resolution or an IPv6 origin route.",
    "Supporting remote SOCKS owner and tunnel_proxy module are partial reads, not whole-file coverage promotions."
  ],
